      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/process/Process_BeanDrain",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Process",
      "name": "Drain the beans",
      "summary": "Draining open beans with several agents at once, as part of the SDLC: build one queue grouped by owner, then take a bean, open it, work it, close it, and take the next — refilling from the deepest queue when a drainer's list runs dry, until nothing drainable…",
      "description": "Draining open beans with several agents at once, as part of the SDLC: build one queue grouped by owner, then take a bean, open it, work it, close it, and take the next — refilling from the deepest queue when a drainer's list runs dry, until nothing drainable is left.\n\nYou are in this process when you are asked to drain beans, when you spawn drainers, or when you pull from a shared queue next to other agents. Each bean still goes through the ordinary OPEN and CLOSE (Process_BeanOpen, Process_BeanClose); what the drain adds is the queue around them, and the rule that a bean another agent holds is skipped, not worked. The queue is advisory: it says who should take a bean, and only OPEN's claim says who did.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "sourcePath": "processes/sdlc/bean-drain.bpmn",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness/blob/main/processes/sdlc/bean-drain.bpmn",
